统旨在主动运行、处理跨应用和服务的任务，而不是等待用户指令，能够访问跨应用、浏览会话和用户活动的数据。\n有望重启智能AI硬件产品线\n智能眼镜是谷歌本届大会最受瞩目的智能硬件产品。\n在5月12日Android Show的新闻发布会上，谷歌表示Android XR智能硬件将在5月19日开幕的年度开发者大会I/O上亮相。\n据报道，谷歌可能会在本次大会上与三星携手首次展示该产品。根据近期泄露信息，这款代号“Jinju”的设备将采用类似MetaRay-Ban的轻量化设计，并搭载Qualcomm Snapdragon AR1芯片、12MP摄像头与定向扬声器系统，整体重量约50g。相比传统头显，这类产品明显更强调日常佩戴属性。\n距离谷歌首次推出Google Glass已过去十余年。市场消息显示，谷歌正与三星、Gentle Monster和Warby Parker合作开发两款AI眼镜:一款是类似MetaRay-Ban的无屏AI眼镜，主打轻量化与日常佩戴，支持免提唤醒Gemini助手;另一款则更为前沿，配备镜片内显示技术，可将导航、实时翻译等信息直接投射在用户视野中。两款眼镜均基于AndroidXR操作系统。\n生态整合能力与商业化进程或许比产品更新更重要\n谷歌一直致力于将Gemini更深入地融入到其生态系统中。除了具体的产品和模型，本次大会还将展示谷歌在AI生态领域的战略布局。\n从议程上看，5月19日的大会将聚焦产品和模型，5月21日的Google Marketing Live则更直接指向广告和商业化。\n报道预计谷歌将在大会上着重介绍人工智能代理的概念和演示，包括即将发布的AI眼镜中的应用案例。\nAndroid 17系统有望迎来变革。Android 17 Beta版或将公布，开放Gemini Nano端侧AI能力，支持第三方开发离线AI应用。全新轻量化系统Aluminum OS或将首秀，融合Android与Chrome OS生态，适配XR设备与笔记本，助力谷歌重返PC市场。\n按照目前多方爆料方向，Gemini或将不再只是独立App，而是嵌入安卓底层的原生能力，形成“Gemini Core”深度嵌入Gmail、Maps、Pixel等核心服务，推动AI从独立工具升级为贯穿全设备的智能系统层。用户可通过快捷入口随时调用，实现跨应用处理事务。与此同时，拥有数十亿用户的Chrome浏览器也有望接入Gemini，提供网页摘要、智能问答乃至自动完成操作的功能。\n谷歌母公司Alphabet此前预计2026财年资本支出将达到1750亿至1850亿美元，这些资金将重点投向大规模数据中心扩建与专用AI算力部署，为Gemini生态系统的落地提供底层支撑，其规模几乎是此前财年的两倍。重金押注AI，谷歌亟需证明其庞大的AI投入能够通过搜索广告、云服务和订阅带来回报。\n(科创板日报 宋子乔)\n\n\n--------\n搜索关键词：谷歌I/O大会 5月19日\n\n网页标题：Google I/O 2026 livestream: When and where to watch Sundar Pichai unveil Gemini AI updates\n\n网页链接：https://www.news9live.com/technology/tech-news/google-i-o-2026-livestream-when-and-where-to-watch-sundar-pichai-unveil-gemini-ai-updates-2972284\n\n发布时间：2026-05-18T16:26:00+08:00\n\n网页内容：Tech News\nGoogle I/O 2026 livestream: When and where to watch Sundar Pichai unveil Gemini AI updates\nPragya Singha Roy Published: 18 May 2026 16:26:PM\nGoogle I/O 2026 will begin on May 19 with Sundar Pichai’s keynote streaming live at 10:30pm IST from Mountain View, California. Google is expected to announce major updates related to Gemini AI, Android XR glasses, AI agents, and its generative AI tools like Veo and Beam.\n![](https://images.news9live.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/12/placeholder.jpg)\nThe company may also share more details about its new Googlebooks laptops, while new Pixel smartphones are unlikely to debut at the event.\nNew Delhi: Google I/O 2026 will be kicking off on May 19th with the company promising to showcase its newest AI, Android, cloud and extended reality (XR) innovations. The two-day developer conference is back in Mountain View, California, at the Shoreline Amphitheatre, with keynote talks from Google CEO Sundar Pichai, DeepMind chief Demis Hassabis, and executives from Google’s Search, Android and Cloud divisions.\nWith Google making significant strides towards the Gemini ecosystem and the introduction of AI-powered consumer products in the past few months, artificial intelligence is anticipated to dominate the event this year. In addition to software updates, the company will likely also be introducing new concepts for Android XR, new AI agents, and some experimental hardware updates. In fact, Google has already announced that there will be live streams throughout the conference of several demos, developer sessions, and talks on AI.\nWhen and where to watch Google I/O 2026 live\nThe keynote session will start at 10am PT (10:30pm IST) on 19th May for Google I/O 2026. It will stream live on Google’s official YouTube channel, as well as on Google’s I/O website.\nGoogle says that the livestream will feature keynote presentations, developer demos, and special sessions on both days of the event. The company is also reviving its “Dialogues” series, which will consist of conversations with industry leaders about the future of AI and new technologies.\nGoogle has also announced that the keynote will be interpreted in American Sign Language (ASL) and streamed separately.\nGemini AI is expected to remain the biggest focus\nGoogle’s Gemini AI platform will likely be at the heart of the focus at this year’s I/O. The company is rumoured to be unveiling a new Gemini model at the keynote, but Google hasn’t officially confirmed the details yet.\nThe company recently unveiled Gemini Intelligence at The Android Show: I/O Edition, showcasing AI agents that were able to execute actions directly on Android mobile devices. At the event, industry observers are anticipating more in-depth integration of Gemini into Google’s Search, Workspace, Android, and Cloud applications.\nGoogle will also be expected to give updates on its far-reaching generative AI portfolio, such as Veo, Lyria and Beam. Veo is Google’s AI video generation model, and Lyria is the AI-generated music. The company’s other futuristic video communication platform is Beam, which projects video calls in a lifelike 3D image.\nAndroid XR glasses and Googlenbooks could also appear\nGoogle’s Android XR, the platform for mixed reality and smart glasses, would be another big focus. The buzz around smart glasses has been building up worldwide for the last year, and Google could show off new features for its Android XR-powered world at I/O 2026.\nThe company also anticipates providing more information about “Googlebooks”, the new line of laptops that is said to be running a new operating system that includes some Android and ChromeOS features. The devices were first teased at Google’s showing earlier this month, which featured Android.\nGoogle doesn’t make big hardware announcements during I/O, with its previous Pixel launches coming in at its yearly “Made by Google” event, which normally happens in August later in the year.\nGoogle\n\n--------\n搜索关键词：谷歌I/O大会 5月19日\n\n网页标题：谷歌I/O开发者大会将至:Gemini迎版本更新，有望重启智能AI硬件产品线_PConline太平洋科技\n\n网页链接：http://m.toutiao.com/group/7641069473411219978/\n\n发布时间：2026-05-18T11:32:15+08:00\n\n网页内容：【太平洋科技快讯】2026年谷歌开发者大会(I/O)将于5月19日—20日在美国加州山景城举办，作为谷歌年度最重要的技术发布会，本届大会聚焦AI大模型、智能硬件与系统生态三大方向，多项重磅更新即将揭晓。\n\n![](https://sf3-ttcdn-tos.pstatp.com/img/tos-cn-i-tjoges91tu/bfbbc8fb5ded8f8766cc0ad28550a287~cs.jpeg)\n本届大会的核心看点之一是Gemini大模型的迭代。自2026年2月推出Gemini 3.1 Pro后，谷歌有望发布Gemini 3.2或3.5版本，大概率不会直接推出Gemini 4.0